.TH FIGLET-FONT-PREVIEW 1 "November 15, 2026"
.SH NAME
figlet-font-preview \- preview text in every installed FIGlet and TOIlet font
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B figlet-font-preview
.RB [ \-\-center " | " \-\-right ]
.RB [ \-\-font\-dir
.IR DIR ]...
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B figlet-font-preview
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B figlet-font-preview
is an interactive terminal program.
It renders a sample text in every FIGlet and TOIlet font it finds,
with a fuzzy-searchable, multi-select font sidebar
for comparing fonts side by side.
.PP
The program parses and renders the font files itself.
It never runs
.BR figlet (6),
so only the font files need to be installed.
.PP
The remaining arguments are joined with spaces to form the initial text.
The default is
.BR Hello .
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be given with one or two leading dashes, for example
.B \-center
or
.BR \-\-center .
.TP
.B \-\-center
Centre the rendered text in the preview.
.TP
.B \-\-right
Right-align the rendered text in the preview.
The default is left; when several of these flags are given, the last one wins.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-dir " DIR"
Also search
.I DIR
for fonts.
May be repeated.
.B \-\-font\-dir=\c
.I DIR
is accepted too.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text, including the default font roots, and exit.
.SH KEYS
.SS Anywhere
.TP
.B tab\fR, \fBshift+tab
Cycle focus: text, search, list.
.TP
.BR pgup ", " pgdn ", " ctrl+u ", " ctrl+d ", mouse wheel"
Scroll the preview.
.TP
.B ctrl+o
Open or close the options pane.
.TP
.B ctrl+y
Copy the cursor font's render to the clipboard as plain text,
wrapped and aligned as shown.
.TP
.B ctrl+s
Save the cursor font's render as a coloured
.IB font .svg
in the current directory.
An existing file is never overwritten; \-2, \-3, ... is added to the name.
.TP
.B ctrl+c
Quit.
.SS Text
.TP
.BR "type" ", " enter
Edit the text.
.B enter
starts a new line.
The box grows to 5 rows, then scrolls.
.SS Search
.TP
.B type
Fuzzy-filter fonts.
.TP
.BR up ", " down
Move in the list.
.TP
.B enter
Select or deselect the highlighted font.
.TP
.B esc
Clear the search.
.SS List
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k ", " g ", " G
Move.
.TP
.BR space ", " enter
Select or deselect.
.TP
.B x
Clear the selection.
.TP
.B /
Jump to the search.
.TP
.B esc
Clear the search.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SS Options pane
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k
Move.
.TP
.BR space ", " enter
Toggle the row.
.TP
.BR left ", " right ", " h ", " l
Change Align, Group by, the background Mode, or a slider's value.
.TP
.B tab
Back to the text, leaving the pane open.
.TP
.BR esc ", " ctrl+o
Close the pane.
.SH FILES
Fonts are read from these directories when they exist:
.RS
.nf
/opt/homebrew/share/figlet
/usr/local/share/figlet
/usr/share/figlet
~/figlet-fonts
.fi
.RE
.PP
On Windows only
.B %USERPROFILE%\efiglet-fonts
and the
.B \-\-font\-dir
directories are searched.
Fonts in different directories are listed separately
even when they are the same font.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR figlet (6),
.BR toilet (1)
